## Detailed Test Procedures

### Test 1: Start Button Functionality
**Objective:** Verify start button initiates motor start sequence

**Procedure:**
1. Enable test mode
2. Simulate start button press
3. Verify contactor output activates
4. Verify running indicator illuminates
5. Verify ready indicator extinguishes
6. Release start button
7. Verify contactor remains latched

**Expected Results:**
- Contact output: ON
- Running indicator: ON
- Ready indicator: OFF
- Latching maintained after button release

### Test 2: Stop Button Functionality
**Objective:** Verify stop button stops motor and resets system

**Procedure:**
1. Start motor (ensure running)
2. Simulate stop button press
3. Verify contactor output deactivates
4. Verify running indicator extinguishes
5. Verify ready indicator illuminates
6. Release stop button
7. Verify system remains in ready state

**Expected Results:**
- Contactor output: OFF
- Running indicator: OFF
- Ready indicator: ON
- System in ready state

### Test 3: Overload Protection
**Objective:** Verify overload protection trips motor

**Procedure:**
1. Start motor (ensure running)
2. Simulate overload condition
3. Verify contactor output deactivates immediately
4. Verify fault indicator illuminates
5. Verify running indicator extinguishes
6. Attempt to restart motor (should fail)
7. Clear overload condition
8. Reset fault condition
9. Verify system returns to ready state

**Expected Results:**
- Immediate contactor deactivation
- Fault indicator: ON
- Motor cannot restart until reset
- System returns to ready after reset

### Test 4: Contactor Feedback Monitoring
**Objective:** Verify contactor feedback monitoring detects faults

**Procedure:**
1. Enable test mode
2. Start motor (ensure running)
3. Simulate loss of contactor feedback
4. Verify fault detection activates
5. Verify contactor output deactivates
6. Restore contactor feedback
7. Reset fault condition
8. Verify system returns to ready state

**Expected Results:**
- Fault detection activates after delay
- Contactor output deactivates
- System cannot restart until reset

### Test 5: Status Indication Verification
**Objective:** Verify all status indicators function correctly

**Procedure:**
1. Test each status indicator individually
2. Verify running indicator only ON when motor running
3. Verify fault indicator only ON when fault condition exists
4. Verify ready indicator only ON when system ready to start
5. Verify indicators don't conflict

**Expected Results:**
- Each indicator operates independently
- No conflicting indicator states
- Indicators reflect actual system state

### Test 6: Latching Functionality
**Objective:** Verify start button latching works correctly

**Procedure:**
1. Press and release start button quickly
2. Verify motor continues running
3. Verify contactor remains latched
4. Test multiple start button presses
5. Verify no chatter or multiple starts

**Expected Results:**
- Single press maintains operation
- No multiple starts from repeated presses
- Stable latching operation

### Test 7: Emergency Stop Integration
**Objective:** Verify emergency stop functionality (if integrated)

**Procedure:**
1. Start motor
2. Activate emergency stop
3. Verify immediate motor stop
4. Verify fault indication
5. Reset emergency stop
6. Reset fault condition
7. Verify system returns to safe state

**Expected Results:**
- Immediate motor stop
- Fault indication
- Cannot restart until reset

## Test I/O Configuration

### Test Inputs
| Tag Name | Address | Data Type | Description |
|----------|---------|-----------|-------------|
| Test_Start_PB | %I4.0 | BOOL | Test start button simulation |
| Test_Stop_PB | %I4.1 | BOOL | Test stop button simulation |
| Test_Overload_PB | %I4.2 | BOOL | Test overload simulation |
| Test_Contactor_FB | %I4.3 | BOOL | Test contactor feedback simulation |
| Test_Mode_Selector | %I4.4 | BOOL | Test mode enable selector |
| Manual_Contactor_Test | %I4.5 | BOOL | Manual contactor test |

### Test Outputs
| Tag Name | Address | Data Type | Description |
|----------|---------|-----------|-------------|
| Simulated_Start_PB | %Q4.0 | BOOL | Simulated start to DOL starter |
| Simulated_Stop_PB | %Q4.1 | BOOL | Simulated stop to DOL starter |
| Simulated_Overload | %Q4.2 | BOOL | Simulated overload to DOL starter |
| Simulated_Aux_Contact | %Q4.3 | BOOL | Simulated aux contact to DOL starter |
| Test_Mode_Active | %Q4.4 | BOOL | Test mode indicator |
| Test_Contactor_Output | %Q4.5 | BOOL | Manual test contactor output |

### Test Status Outputs
| Tag Name | Address | Data Type | Description |
|----------|---------|-----------|-------------|
| Running_Verified | %Q5.0 | BOOL | Running status verified |
| Fault_Verified | %Q5.1 | BOOL | Fault status verified |
| Ready_Verified | %Q5.2 | BOOL | Ready status verified |
| Test_Success_Latch | %Q5.3 | BOOL | Test passed indication |
| Test_Fail_Latch | %Q5.4 | BOOL | Test failed indication |

## Test Timing Requirements
- Start button response: < 100ms
- Stop button response: < 50ms
- Overload response: < 50ms
- Contactor feedback timeout: 500ms
- Status indication response: < 100ms

## Test Sequence Order
1. Power-up test
2. Status indication test
3. Start button test
4. Stop button test
5. Latching test
6. Overload protection test
7. Contactor feedback test
8. Integration test
9. Documentation and results

## Pass/Fail Criteria
- **Pass:** All test procedures meet expected results
- **Fail:** Any test procedure does not meet expected results
- **Conditional:** Test passes with minor deviations documented

## Test Documentation
- Record test date and time
- Document test personnel
- Note any deviations from expected results
- Record software/firmware versions
- Document hardware configuration
- Save test results for traceability

## Safety Considerations During Testing
- Ensure emergency stop is functional
- Verify all safety interlocks are active
- Use test mode to prevent unexpected equipment operation
- Have personnel clear of equipment during testing
- Follow lockout/tagout procedures when required
- Test in controlled environment before field deployment

## Troubleshooting Test Failures
| Symptom | Possible Cause | Action |
|---------|----------------|--------|
| Motor won't start in test | Test mode not enabled | Enable test mode |
| Contactor feedback test fails | Wiring issue | Check aux contact wiring |
| Overload test doesn't trip | Overload setting incorrect | Adjust overload setting |
| Status indicators incorrect | Logic error | Review SCL implementation |
| Latching doesn't work | Contact fault | Check contactor contact |

